name: add-printer-popup-feasibility
description: "2026-10-20 feasibility of the canvas 3-step \"Add a printer\" popup replacing run_wizard in the printer chat; what Orca can and can't supply, 5 decisions asked of Kenneth."
metadata:
  node_type: memory
  type: project
  originSessionId: 2e4c8ad1-82aa-46c8-8b45-2bdab5d28d27
  modified: 2026-10-20T22:28:20.500Z
---

Worktree `.claude/worktrees/add-printer-popup` (removed 2026-10-21), branch `claude/add-printer-popup` off jusprin-newui 1cbce387d8. Feasibility reported 2026-10-20; nothing built until Kenneth answers.

Verified facts (file:line in the report):
- Network finds are Bambu only. `discover_printers()` hides LAN printers with no access code (upstream `get_my_machine_list` filter); the fuller list is `get_local_machinelist()`. SSDP needs the plug-in AND the Bambu agent active (only when a Bambu preset is selected). Non-Bambu scans (Bonjour/_octoprint, Creality, Flashforge) run only from PhysicalPrinterDialog's Browse.
- `add_printer` accepts a device_id and records the link, but nothing passes one. Nozzle unknown before connecting.
- Plate: `curr_bed_type` is project-level. Orca remembers `printer_settings[<name>].curr_bed_type` per printer name, then falls back to hidden `default_bed_type` (numeric only; text falls back to High Temp). Plate dropdown only for Bambu or `support_multi_bed_types` (MK4 and Ender 3 V2: off). No "Satin"/"Smooth PEI".
- Filament: "Common on" has no data; `default_materials` is the closest (MK4 = 10 Prusa Generic). Prusament profiles are compatible only with CORE One. Tray sync needs a connected printer.
- Catalog: 64 brands / 383 models; nozzle sets vary (1 to 8 sizes), so no fixed 4-button control; SecKit/Seckit brand split.
- The design boards draw no Back/Next/Cancel, and their examples conflict (Ender 3 V2 vs MK4).

Recommended (pending Kenneth): passive Bambu-only list; plate step only where Orca offers plates, saved via `select_bed_type`; step 3 = "Which filament do you want to start with?" + "Suggested for the <model>"; controls added in code first; the native error fallback keeps run_wizard.

Related: [[filament-chip-no-spool-decisions]], [[jusprin-chip-orca-seams]], [[design-source-is-claude-artifacts]], [[printer-conversation-panel-19b]].

**Built 2026-10-20 (uncommitted, worktree above):** Kenneth took all 5 recommendations, then approved the filament-step redesign (design session's artifact https://claude.ai/artifact/Kytv8cHPVQdN1ajW2K96N1; canvas v38 + Design System v29 updated to match). Step 3 = "Your filaments" / "Suggested for the <model>" (profile default first) / "Every filament for the <model>"; at the end a "Show filaments made for other printers" tick box (picking one saves an OrcaSlicer clone_presets_for_filament copy "<alias> @<printer>" into slot 1) and "Create a filament preset…" (adds the printer, fires EVT_CREATE_FILAMENT, puts the new preset in slot 1). Options come from SetupOptionsLoader (scratch PresetBundle via the new neutral seam PresetBundle::load_system_vendor_from_dir; upstream's later load_vendors does the same, see the comment at the site). Native page-failure fallback keeps run_wizard (action orca_printer_list).
